# atlas_preview_routes.test.Caddyfile — throwaway config for
# caddy/test/atlas_routes_local.sh: the REAL atlas snippet
# (../atlas_preview_routes.caddy), HTTP-only, on a free port -- so it runs on
# this laptop's homebrew caddy, which has no jwtauth plugin (no Docker, no Go
# here either). That means this proves ROUTING only, never the Cloudflare
# Access gate in front of it in production; caddy/test/run.sh (on the server,
# against the real image) proves the auth half.
#
# ATLAS_TEST_PORT and ATLAS_PREVIEW_ROOT are env vars the script sets — the
# latter is the SAME knob atlas_preview_routes.caddy itself reads (see its
# `root` line), so production and this test share one file with one seam.
#
# The trailing `respond 404` models "nothing else in this vhost matched" — in
# production that is preview_routes.caddy's landing-page catch-all `handle`,
# which also never hands back real file content for a path this block does
# not own. `handle` blocks are mutually exclusive with what follows once
# matched, so this line never fires for a request the snippet above handled.
{
	auto_https off
	admin off
}

:{$ATLAS_TEST_PORT:19999} {
	import ../atlas_preview_routes.caddy
	respond 404
}
